<title>JAPAN: Japan July soybean imports up 4.85 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan July soybean imports up 4.85 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in July totalled 445,079 tonnes, up by 4.85 percent from a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			July 96	 June 96     July 95</p>
<p> Total imports    445,079	 440,072     424,472</p>
<p>Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		 311,028	 274,775     276,039</p>
<p> Brazil		94,522	  88,882     101,485</p>
<p> Paraguay	    25,781	  42,511	   nil</p>
<p> China		  9,895	  16,702	18,685</p>
</text>
